-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Elite
  Publisher   Firebird, 1985
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        ELITE128.TAP
  MD5         213ca5957154bf1d3aa5b72448628ef2

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu and the Next start-up. Game
  logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.0: the standard release from its tape, original look and pace;
              50 fps title ship; Elite.scr loading screen from ENTER

  Note        The ELITE128 tape, the original Firebird release (a 48K game,
              the same code at other addresses): it starts at "Load New
              Commander (Y/N)?". Its own interrupt table already works on the
              Next; the smooth title ship is the only change. Original look
              and 3.5 MHz. The title screens' rotating ship is redrawn every
              frame (50 fps) at the original turning speed by the game's own
              draw. Keys: M / N roll, S / X pitch, SPACE / SYMBOL SHIFT faster
              / slower, A laser, T / F target / fire missile, 1-4 views (1
              launches), H hyperspace, I / O charts, K market, L status, P
              data, ENTER inventory. Known issues: hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  No cheats.

